<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284015c9b1a86f144f15794ca2eac524de6d2294466427c76ee4bef612ffccfb</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's ex-spy chief arrested for espionage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f3899a9fd1a790c970167482212b8cd90010f9db401073fb99f72978880daa1</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-espionage/a-79560278--e631ff19ef7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-espionage/a-79560278?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">August Hanning, the man who once led Germany's spy service, is now under investigation for passing on state secrets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Far-right AfD gets first house speaker in a German state parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad6a9ef9c7fbc551b2e0d23f117c5f11437c6bb73b81c79b1bb089aa9b84f466</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497--5fb1cf58f705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since World War II, a far-right party has a house speaker in a German state parliament. And Germany's foreign minister has warned that the climate crisis could fuel extremism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b990b9b0ff82cab05e56c9dcbe782d003acbedead5523505ca75d3339c73498</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Spy chief warns Russia conflict risk growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3046c879983666fc7abe32b48224208f11c59e4cd85f7d71fcb3d7eb0d4f0ab0</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789--3bde17a9e96c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is already waging a "shadow war" against Europe, the head of Germany's foreign intelligence service says. The Left Party is taking a case over remarks by the CDU's Katherina Reiche to a top court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96a076eebd0cfebe0b10b40d5c83bb02e0fd519327e91102ba41f608af7fa7aa</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD makes history again in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2447d431cc6a8e9426b088fb98cbca9a7737976d9e79ed20977c09aab8a49676</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146--3b11bbf1dc05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-makes-history-again-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79565146?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since the end of World War II, a German state parliament has chosen parliamentary speaker from the far right: Tobias Rausch of the Alternative for Germany (AfD).</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-07T06:11:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
